WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.406
Teacher midterm practice, question 15.

2
00:00:04.026 --> 00:00:06.853
In Figure 1, the modulus of resilience can be

3
00:00:06.853 --> 00:00:10.084
approximated by the area bounded by which points?

4
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:14.869
The modulus of resilience is the energy absorbed up to

5
00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:18.640
yielding: the area under the elastic part of the curve.

6
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.112
The elastic region ends at B, and G is the strain at B.

7
00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:26.088
So the area is the triangle O, B, G.

8
00:00:26.708 --> 00:00:29.792
O, A, G stops halfway up the elastic line,

9
00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:32.590
and the larger areas include plastic work.

10
00:00:34.191 --> 00:00:36.325
The answer is B: O, B, G.

11
00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:39.412
Resilience is the elastic area only.

12
00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:42.101
The area under the whole curve is toughness.
